---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Solar Panel Installation Thailand | Residential & Commercial PV Systems | JJ Com Solar Cell';
const description = 'Professional solar panel installation across Thailand. Rooftop and ground-mount photovoltaic systems for homes and businesses. Monocrystalline and polycrystalline PV modules, 10+ years experience, free quote.';
---
<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="website"
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Solar Panel Installation",
    "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "Thailand" }
  }}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-solar-green">Home</a> / <span>Services</span> / <span>Solar Panel Installation</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-solar-yellow/20 text-solar-yellow px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-6">
        Serving Thailand Since 2016
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Solar Panel Installation</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Complete rooftop and ground-mount photovoltaic systems for residential and commercial properties across Thailand.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">500+</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Installations completed</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">1-3</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Days typical install time</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">25yr</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Panel performance warranty</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How Solar Panel Installation Works</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Solar panel installation is the process of mounting photovoltaic modules on your roof or ground structure, connecting them to an inverter, and integrating the system with your building's electrical supply. The goal is to convert sunlight into usable electricity that reduces or eliminates your dependence on the Provincial Electricity Authority (PEA) grid.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        We install two main types of photovoltaic modules: monocrystalline and polycrystalline. Monocrystalline panels use single-crystal silicon cells that achieve higher efficiency, typically 20% to 22%, making them ideal for properties with limited roof space. Polycrystalline panels use multiple silicon fragments melted together, offering slightly lower efficiency at 17% to 19% but at a lower cost per watt. For most Thai homes, we recommend monocrystalline panels due to their superior performance in high temperatures and smaller footprint.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Each solar cell within a module generates approximately 0.5 volts DC. Multiple cells wired in series create the panel's rated voltage, while parallel strings increase current capacity. A typical residential system strings 10 to 20 panels in series, producing 400 to 600 volts DC that feeds into a grid-tie or hybrid inverter. The inverter converts this DC power to 220V AC at 50Hz, matching Thailand's electrical standards, and synchronises with the grid for seamless net metering.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Panel Types We Install</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Monocrystalline Silicon Modules</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Highest efficiency panels using single-crystal silicon wafers. Dark uniform appearance. Better heat tolerance than polycrystalline, meaning less power loss on hot Thai afternoons. Typical output: 400 to 550 watts per panel. Best for homes with limited roof area or high electricity demand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Polycrystalline Silicon Modules</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Cost-effective option using multiple silicon crystals. Blue speckled appearance. Slightly larger footprint for the same wattage but lower upfront cost. Typical output: 330 to 450 watts per panel. Suitable for properties with ample roof space and moderate energy budgets.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why Proper Installation Matters in Thailand</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Thailand's tropical climate demands installation practices that differ from temperate countries. Ambient temperatures of 30 to 40 degrees Celsius cause solar panels to operate at 50 to 65 degrees Celsius on the cell surface. At these temperatures, standard panels lose 10% to 15% of their rated output due to the negative temperature coefficient of silicon. We account for this thermal derating in our system sizing, ensuring your installed capacity exceeds your nominal requirement.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Monsoon season brings another challenge. From May through October, heavy rainfall and cloud cover can reduce daily generation by 40% to 60% compared to dry season peaks. Properly designed arrays with appropriate tilt angles self-clean during rain, but shading from overhanging trees becomes critical when the sun sits lower in the sky. Our site surveys include year-round shade analysis to prevent unexpected production drops.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Coastal and island installations face salt spray that corrodes aluminium frames and electrical connections over time. We use marine-grade anodised aluminium frames, stainless steel mounting hardware, and dielectric grease on all electrical terminals. These measures add decades to system life in Koh Chang, Pattaya, Phuket, and other coastal locations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What You Get with Our Installation Service</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Free site survey:</strong> We assess roof structure, orientation, shading patterns, and electrical capacity. Shade analysis using solar pathfinder tools identifies obstruction angles for all seasons.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>System design:</strong> Custom array layout optimised for your roof geometry and energy consumption. We calculate tilt angle, azimuth, and string configuration for maximum annual yield.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Tier 1 panels:</strong> We supply monocrystalline and polycrystalline modules from manufacturers with proven bankability and 25-year performance warranties. All panels IEC 61215 and IEC 61730 certified.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Professional mounting:</strong> Corrosion-resistant aluminium racking, stainless steel fasteners, and waterproof roof penetrations. Systems engineered for 150 km/h wind loads and seismic requirements.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Inverter integration:</strong> Grid-tie, hybrid, or off-grid inverter matched to your array size and energy goals. Includes DC cabling, combiner boxes, and AC distribution panel connections.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Grid connection:</strong> We handle net metering application with PEA, including single-line diagrams, electrical permits, and utility inspection coordination.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Monitoring setup:</strong> WiFi or 4G monitoring gateway, smartphone app configuration, and performance baseline recording. Track generation from day one.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>1-year maintenance:</strong> Free annual inspection, cleaning, and performance verification included. Panel cleaning at 300 THB per panel thereafter.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Installation Process</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 text-center">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-solar-green text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3 font-bold">1</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Site Survey</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Free on-site assessment of roof, shading, and electrical system. Shade analysis and structural load check.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 text-center">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-solar-green text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3 font-bold">2</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">System Design</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Custom panel layout, inverter sizing, and electrical schematic. Net metering documentation prepared.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 text-center">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-solar-green text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3 font-bold">3</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Installation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Professional mounting, wiring, and inverter installation. Typically 1 to 3 days for residential systems.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 text-center">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-solar-green text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3 font-bold">4</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Commissioning</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Testing, grid connection, PEA inspection, and monitoring activation. Full handover with performance report.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Residential vs Commercial Installations</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-3">Residential Systems</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">Typical size: 3 to 10 kilowatt-peak. Rooftop installation on concrete, metal, or tile roofs. Grid-tie or hybrid configuration with optional battery backup. Net metering reduces electricity bills by 70% to 90% for most Thai homes.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Payback period: 5 to 7 years in Thailand, depending on location and electricity consumption. Systems are eligible for net metering credits through PEA.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-3">Commercial Systems</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">Typical size: 20 to 500+ kilowatt-peak. Rooftop, carport, or ground-mount arrays. Three-phase inverters with power factor correction. Monitoring dashboard for sustainability reporting and power purchase agreements.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Corporate clients benefit from accelerated depreciation, green marketing credentials, and protection against rising electricity tariffs. We structure power purchase agreements (PPAs) where appropriate.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">How long does installation take?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Most residential installations take 1 to 3 days after permits are approved. Commercial projects vary by size, typically 1 to 4 weeks. PEA grid connection approval adds 2 to 4 weeks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Do I need a new roof?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Not necessarily. We assess roof condition during the site survey. Most existing concrete and metal roofs can support solar arrays. Tile roofs may require reinforcement for large systems. We do not install on roofs with significant damage or leaks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Will installation damage my roof?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">No. We use industry-standard mounting systems with EPDM rubber flashings and waterproof sealants. All penetrations are tested for leaks before commissioning. Our waterproofing warranty covers 5 years.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">How much can I save?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A typical 5 kilowatt-peak residential system in Thailand generates 6,000 to 7,500 kWh annually. At PEA rates of 4 to 5.5 THB per unit for high-consumption households, annual savings range from 24,000 to 41,000 THB. Net metering further improves returns by crediting excess exports.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/guides/solar-sunlight-hours" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Sunlight Hours in Thailand</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Discover which months deliver peak solar generation</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">System Sizing Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Calculate the right kilowatt-peak capacity for your home</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-solar-green text-white rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Ready to Go Solar?</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">Get a free site survey and personalised quote for your solar panel installation across Thailand.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block bg-white text-solar-green font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
        Get a Free Quote
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm mt-4 opacity-80">
        Based in <a href="/" class="underline">Koh Chang</a>, serving all of Thailand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
